<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Balwant Singh of Bharatpur</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/1826">1826</a>–<a href="/years/1853">1853</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Balwant Singh was the Jat <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharaja">Maharaja</a> of Bharatpur from 1826 to 1853. As a child he was displaced by his cousin Durjan Sal in a succession dispute, and the British, under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stapleton-cotton-1st-viscount-combermere">Lord Combermere</a>, besieged and stormed the fortress of Bharatpur in January 1826 and restored him to the throne. His state remained in alliance with the British for the rest of his reign.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/balwant-singh-of-bharatpur.jpg" alt="Balwant Singh of Bharatpur" width="320" height="483" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Maharaja_Balwant_Singh.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
